"<header class=\"topbar\">\n    <div class=\"wrap\">\n      <a class=\"wordmark\" href=\"/\" aria-label=\"Lotolipi home\">lotolipi<span>.</span></a>\n      <nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a><a href=\"/#case-studies\">Case studies</a><a href=\"/lottolov\">Lottolov</a><a href=\"/resume\">Résumé</a><a href=\"/#contact\">Contact</a></nav>\n    </div>\n  </header><main id=\"main-content\"><section class=\"hero wrap\"><p class=\"label\"><a href=\"/#case-studies\">Case studies</a> / Decision support</p><h1>Signal<span>.</span></h1><p class=\"hero-intro\">Should NOVA pilot a premium beverage? I designed a workspace that lets a decision-maker follow a claim back to its source and see how a change in sales volume affects the recommendation.</p><a class=\"hero-link\" href=\"/signal\">Try the prototype →</a></section><section class=\"work\"><div class=\"wrap\"><header class=\"work-head\"><p class=\"label\">Independent prototype · Synthetic research</p><h2>Two numbers, two questions.</h2><p>67.2% of respondents aged 18–34 expressed concept interest. A separate sample returned a 24% positive response at ₹99. The studies cannot tell us how that age group would respond at that price.</p></header><figure><img src=\"/assets/signal-brief.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:650px;object-fit:cover;object-position:top\" alt=\"Decision Brief with source-linked concept interest and price response\"></figure><div class=\"walkthrough-copy\"><h3>Keep the interpretation with the evidence.</h3><p>In Evidence Room, the reader can inspect both samples, open the source rows and compare the records. Reconcile lets them save “Context differs” with a rationale and the evidence versions behind it.</p><h3>Make the decision testable.</h3><p>In Alternatives, reducing pilot volume from 250,000 to 200,000 units moves the model from ₹5 lakh profit to ₹2 lakh loss. A reviewer can revise that assumption and return to the original reading.</p><h3>What I verified</h3><p>Desktop and mobile browser tests covered source inspection, saving a rationale, changing the forecast and retrieving saved work after reload. These results describe prototype behaviour. The business figures are synthetic.</p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/signal\">Explore Signal →</a></div></div></section></main>"